                              Spring Events ke advanced concepts
1️⃣ Order in Listeners :
   - Jab ek hi event ko multiple listeners handle karte hain,toh kaun pehle chalega aur kaun baad me — usko decide karna = Listener Order.
   - By default → Order guaranteed nahi hota.
   - Use Case,
         Order create hua:
                        - Pehle Inventory update ho
                        - Fir Payment process ho
                        - Fir Email send ho.
   - Example :
             @EventListener
             @Order(1)
             public void updateInventory(OrderCreatedEvent event) {
                 System.out.println("Inventory Updated");
             }

             @EventListener
             @Order(2)
             public void sendEmail(OrderCreatedEvent event) {
                 System.out.println("Email Sent");
             }
   - Rule: Smaller number = higher priority (pehle chalega).


2️⃣ Async Event Listeners :
           - Default me events synchronous hote hain.matlab publisher rukta hai jab tak listener ka kaam complete na ho.
           - Async ka matlab: Background me chale, Publisher wait na kare.
           - Use Case :
                     - Order create hua,Email bhejna 3 sec lag raha hai,Tum nahi chahte order creation slow ho.
           - Example :
                    @Async
                    @EventListener
                    public void sendEmail(OrderCreatedEvent event) {
                        System.out.println("Sending Email...");
                    }

3️⃣ Conditional Event Listeners :
                 - Event aaye lekin condition true ho tab hi listener chale.
                 - Use Case : Agar order amount > 10,000,tabhi premium email bhejna hai.
                 - Example :
                          @EventListener(condition = "#event.amount > 10000")
                          public void premiumCustomerNotification(OrderCreatedEvent event) {
                              System.out.println("Premium Email Sent");
                          }


4️⃣ Global Error Handling in Listeners :
  - Problem : Agar ek listener me exception aa gaya toh baaki listeners ruk sakte hain (sync case me)
  - Solution :
              Custom Error Handler (Best Way for Async).

              @Bean
              public ApplicationEventMulticaster applicationEventMulticaster() {
                  SimpleApplicationEventMulticaster multicaster =
                          new SimpleApplicationEventMulticaster();

                  multicaster.setErrorHandler(error ->
                          System.out.println("Global Error: " + error.getMessage()));

                  return multicaster;
              }